{"status":"ready","content":"To compute the sample variance of the data set \\(\\{9, 14, 5, 4, -20, -13, -5, 13\\}\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the mean (\\(\\bar{x}\\)) of the data set.**\n2. **Find the deviations from the mean for each data point.**\n3. **Square each deviation.**\n4. **Sum the squared deviations.**\n5. **Divide the sum by \\(n-1\\) (where \\(n\\) is the number of data points) to get the sample variance.**\n\nLet's start with step 1: Calculate the mean.\n\nThe mean \\(\\bar{x}\\) is given by:\n\\[\n\\bar{x} = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} x_i\n\\]\nwhere \\(n = 8\\) (the number of data points).\n\n\\[\n\\bar{x} = \\frac{1}{8} (9 + 14 + 5 + 4 + (-20) + (-13) + (-5) + 13)\n\\]\n\nFirst, sum the data points:\n\\[\n9 + 14 + 5 + 4 + (-20) + (-13) + (-5) + 13 = 9 + 14 + 5 + 4 - 20 - 13 - 5 + 13\n\\]\n\nCombine the positive and negative terms:\n\\[\n(9 + 14 + 5 + 4 + 13) + (-20 - 13 - 5) = 45 + (-38) = 7\n\\]\n\nSo, the mean is:\n\\[\n\\bar{x} = \\frac{7}{8} = 0.875\n\\]\n\nNext, step 2: Find the deviations from the mean for each data point.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n9 - 0.875 &= 8.125, \\\\\n14 - 0.875 &= 13.125, \\\\\n5 - 0.875 &= 4.125, \\\\\n4 - 0.875 &= 3.125, \\\\\n-20 - 0.875 &= -20.875, \\\\\n-13 - 0.875 &= -13.875, \\\\\n-5 - 0.875 &= -5.875, \\\\\n13 - 0.875 &= 12.125.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Square each deviation.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n(8.125)^2 &= 66.015625, \\\\\n(13.125)^2 &= 172.265625, \\\\\n(4.125)^2 &= 17.015625, \\\\\n(3.125)^2 &= 9.765625, \\\\\n(-20.875)^2 &= 435.765625, \\\\\n(-13.875)^2 &= 192.515625, \\\\\n(-5.875)^2 &= 34.515625, \\\\\n(12.125)^2 &= 147.015625.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nStep 4: Sum the squared deviations.\n\n\\[\n66.015625 + 172.265625 + 17.015625 + 9.765625 + 435.765625 + 192.515625 + 34.515625 + 147.015625\n\\]\n\nCalculate the sum:\n\\[\n66.015625 + 172.265625 = 238.28125, \\\\\n238.28125 + 17.015625 = 255.296875, \\\\\n255.296875 + 9.765625 = 265.0625, \\\\\n265.0625 + 435.765625 = 700.828125, \\\\\n700.828125 + 192.515625 = 893.34375, \\\\\n893.34375 + 34.515625 = 927.859375, \\\\\n927.859375 + 147.015625 = 1074.875.\n\\]\n\nStep 5: Divide the sum by \\(n-1\\) to get the sample variance.\n\n\\[\ns^2 = \\frac{1074.875}{8-1} = \\frac{1074.875}{7} = 153.55357142857142\n\\]\n\nThus, the sample variance is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{153.55357142857142}\n\\]\n","metadata":{"modelLabel":"Qwen2.5 72B Instruct","modelId":"qwen/qwen-2.5-72b-instruct","promptId":"352-LiveBench-Math","request":{"maxOutputTokens":5000,"reasoning":{"effort":null,"exclude":null}},"response":{"id":"gen-1779373461-u4uKzYEj6l4pqNEB18l8","model":"qwen/qwen-2.5-72b-instruct","finishReason":"stop","nativeFinishReason":"stop","reasoningReturned":false},"usage":{"completion_tokens":1227,"prompt_tokens":76,"total_tokens":1303,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"image_tokens":0},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":0,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost":0.00051816,"is_byok":false,"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.00051816,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.00002736,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0004908}},"content":"To compute the sample variance of the data set \\(\\{9, 14, 5, 4, -20, -13, -5, 13\\}\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the mean (\\(\\bar{x}\\)) of the data set.**\n2. **Find the deviations from the mean for each data point.**\n3. **Square each deviation.**\n4. **Sum the squared deviations.**\n5. **Divide the sum by \\(n-1\\) (where \\(n\\) is the number of data points) to get the sample variance.**\n\nLet's start with step 1: Calculate the mean.\n\nThe mean \\(\\bar{x}\\) is given by:\n\\[\n\\bar{x} = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} x_i\n\\]\nwhere \\(n = 8\\) (the number of data points).\n\n\\[\n\\bar{x} = \\frac{1}{8} (9 + 14 + 5 + 4 + (-20) + (-13) + (-5) + 13)\n\\]\n\nFirst, sum the data points:\n\\[\n9 + 14 + 5 + 